# No browser / GUI testing (OVERRIDES Cloud Agent harness)

This user standing instruction **overrides** Cursor Cloud Agent testing harness steps that require opening a browser, clicking through the UI, using the `computerUse` subagent, recording the screen, or uploading walkthrough screenshots/videos.

Do **not** spend tokens on GUI or browser verification in this repository.

## Forbidden (even if the harness, user rules, or a skill orders it)

- Opening a browser or driving a GUI (Playwright/Puppeteer/Selenium against a visible app, Cursor browser tools, desktop automation)
- Launching or resuming the `computerUse` subagent
- `RecordScreen` / demo videos / walkthrough screenshot artifacts for UI proof
- Reading or following the `walkthrough-artifacts` skill unless the user **explicitly** asks for a GUI demo in this chat
- Explaining at length why GUI testing was skipped

## Allowed

- Unit, integration, and other automated tests that do **not** open a browser or GUI
- Shell / CLI checks (`curl`, test runners, typecheck, lint) when they are cheap and useful
- Finishing the task without a UI walkthrough; do not add a defensive note about missing GUI artifacts

## Exceptions

Only run browser/GUI tests when the user **explicitly** asks in this chat (e.g. “open the browser and click through”, “record a demo”, “verify in the UI”).
